&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Unifying newly acquired companies into the core Abacus technical environment. You’ll&amp;nbsp;handle the technical heavy lifting—migrating Microsoft 365 tenants, moving identities&amp;nbsp;(SSO), consolidating file storage, and merging communication tools.&amp;nbsp;As part of a newly forming team, your initial focus will span both M&amp;amp;A execution and&amp;nbsp;foundational platform engineering. This will involve supporting the Abacus hosted&amp;nbsp;services, endpoint environments, and end‑user experience. Focuses on automation,&amp;nbsp;standardization, security posture. This will be temporarily as these services transition toanother team.&amp;nbsp;Once fully established, your focus will center on unifying newly acquired companies intothe Abacus environment: migrating Microsoft 365 tenants, moving identities (SSO),&amp;nbsp;consolidating file storage, and merging communication tools.&amp;nbsp;Equally important to the technical execution is clear, proactive communication. A smooth&amp;nbsp;migration depends on preparing incoming teams for what’s changing, setting&amp;nbsp;expectations, and guiding them through Day 1.&amp;nbsp;We don&#39;t expect you to be a deep subject matter expert in every single technology on day&amp;nbsp;one. What we do need is a versatile engineer with strong foundational knowledge of&amp;nbsp;modern Microsoft cloud ecosystems, identity tools, and migration workflows who enjoys&amp;nbsp;solving practical IT integration problems.&amp;nbsp;As M&amp;amp;A cutovers must take place with minimal downtime to business operations, this role&amp;nbsp;does require some flexibility in working hours, including scheduled evening and weekend&amp;nbsp;work during migration windows. Flexible time off during standard working hours will be&amp;nbsp;coordinated in return.&lt;/p&gt;
