&lt;td width=&quot;623&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The&amp;nbsp;Escalation Engineer&amp;nbsp;is a senior Tier 3 engineering role within the&amp;nbsp;Service&amp;nbsp;Delivery&amp;nbsp;organization, acting as the primary technical owner and escalation authority for a&amp;nbsp;portfolio of high-visibility, high-touch clients.&amp;nbsp;Beyond&amp;nbsp;resolving complex incidents,&amp;nbsp;the role&amp;nbsp;is&amp;nbsp;responsible&amp;nbsp;for&amp;nbsp;preventing them,&amp;nbsp;driving stability, operational maturity, and long-term technical improvement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating at the intersection of infrastructure engineering, service operations, and client advisory, the&amp;nbsp;Technical&amp;nbsp;Account&amp;nbsp;Manager&amp;nbsp;delivers proactive technical leadership across client environments and the shared multi-tenant platform.&amp;nbsp;Unlike traditional escalation support, this position functions as a trusted technical partner to both the client and internal teams.&amp;nbsp;The&amp;nbsp;Technical&amp;nbsp;Account&amp;nbsp;Manager&amp;nbsp;maintains&amp;nbsp;deep familiarity with assigned environments and provides white-glove service, ensuring consistent standards, effective troubleshooting, and durable resolutions.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td width=&quot;623&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td width=&quot;623&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the senior escalation point for Tier 1 and Tier 2 Service Desk administrators for assigned clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to calls/emails/messages from technical POC’s from assigned clients in a timely and efficient manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with SME engineering teams to uphold operational and architectural standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote documentation, knowledge sharing, and service continuity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take full ownership of complex or business-critical incidents through permanent resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead incident bridges and coordinate internal and external stakeholders during major outages for assigned clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with assigned clients CXM on a regular basis to discuss ongoing issues, trends, and technical road map&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear status communication and expectation management throughout incident lifecycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform root cause analysis and implement preventative remediation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain regular updates for active incidents and projects in ServiceNow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify systemic risks and drive proactive remediation across client environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business requirements into technical recommendations and improvement roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with client stakeholders and advocate for client outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in a rotating out-of-hours escalation schedule&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work shifts between 7:00am and 6:00pm, including coverage during team absences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasionally perform planned maintenance and project work during evenings and weekends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
