&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Project Manager of Incident Response, you will be primarily dedicated to external, client-facing projects within our Incident Response team. You will be the driving force behind successful, thorough, and robust project deliverables that result in progressive change and secure enhancements to our client’s technical environments. As the primary face of the team on client calls, you will field questions, establish trust, and set precedent as the go-to person for all incident-related matters. You will be tasked with understanding the current state of an incident, establishing ownership of the overall direction of containment and recovery, and ensuring all parties are aligned with the verticals defined. Constantly in sync with the primary lead engineer leading containment and recovery strategies and delivering agreed-upon strategic initiatives to all parties, you will work as part of a dynamic, flexing team – ready to respond at a moment’s notice mapping into your team&#39;s on-call rotation. This position will report directly to our Director of Incident Response PMO.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities (including, but not limited to):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Project Management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinates multiple, external technical projects from inception to completion:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follows established core processes, project templates, and methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Takes a lead in Professional Services stand-ups &amp;amp; meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborates on project planning, project design, preparation of deliverables, timelining, and contingency planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understands SOW requirements and converts them into realistic, executable project plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages the project resources to effectively execute on-time deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tracks and manages the project budget from the outset through successful completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tracks and oversees T&amp;amp;M project scope and related time entries, confirming their validity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employs creative measures to keep project scope contained&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures QA standards are being met before project delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outlines goals, strategy, and execution with Abacus’s engineers:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assists in the initial triage and establishment of access for project kick-off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drives team’s development of project proposals and scope documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverages conflict management techniques to address disagreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assigns and aligns necessary resources, understanding resource requirements and capacity (perm or contracted) on projects, maximizing available resources and leveraging each engineer’s skill set effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follows up with engineers on a weekly, daily, or (when necessary) hourly basis to understand the progress of their assigned work and to identify potential roadblocks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitors and summarizes progress of project(s) to stakeholders:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company Leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client Contacts and IR Partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sets and conducts status meetings with client contacts, keeping them informed of progress and setting proper expectations
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads the creation of PowerPoint presentations and project reports as required for large projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participates in incident response on-call rotation for incoming IR projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifies and understands when it is necessary to escalate issues to higher-level resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Addresses billing disputes, overruns, and customer service issues with meaningful resolutions, looping in additional Entara resources as necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conducts post-mortems to outline lessons learned and improve internal processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Problem Solving&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Becomes an active part of project teams solving technical or business roadblocks until a resolution is reached and the outcome is personally verified&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perseveres in making sound judgment calls when lacking one or more desired resources or data points&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenges technical or business requirements ensuring that we deliver the right solution, at the right price, at the right time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverages and employs an understanding of intermediate to advanced systems configuration, management, and maintenance in areas including the following &lt;em&gt;(this is a sample but not exhaustive listing of work areas and project tasks assigned to our IR-focused engineers&lt;/em&gt;):&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Microsoft-related technologies: Windows Server, Exchange, SQL Server, SharePoint, Active Directory, GPO, LAPS, SCCM, MDT, Intune, 0365, Azure etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Virtualization technologies: VMware and Microsoft Hyper V
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Restore and reimage virtual servers from images and various backup solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Restore and rebuild ESX and Hyper-V hosts, domain controller, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mount ISOs to virtual systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Upload virtual templates to any hypervisor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Out of Band access to Physical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage console access such as ILO and iDrac to establish remote connection to offline physical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backup and disaster recovery solutions for both desktops and servers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access solutions: VPN, Remote Desktop, Citrix, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnostic tools; review event logs, Syslogs, monitoring data, and memory dumps to troubleshoot issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security-enhancing solutions for systems and applications (including MFA and endpoint protection).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Metrics Measuring Success&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintains billable utilization targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures all mandatory reports are generated and updated daily&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meets or exceeds deadlines for all assigned projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keeps projects profitable while not skimping on quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverages cost variance and schedule variance formulas to measure project success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributes to the team’s attainment of high customer satisfaction scores on project delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Records complete change details, time worked entries, and work notes in ServiceNow in real-time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifies opportunities for process improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Following Process&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follows Abacus’s project process to execute project deliverables: configure, test, implement, refine, document, monitor, and transition to appropriate stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follows Abacus’s Change Management Process to perform approved changes in client environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicates internally and (as directed) externally to provide timely information regarding project status, promised follow-ups, and requested feedback on a detailed and professional basis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a knowledge seeker. Regardless of method, you have obtained and exposed yourself to knowledge centers that have qualified you to master technical project delivery and the systems engineering required to successfully recover, deploy, and enhance infrastructures. You ideally have a four-year degree in a relevant field and are working towards or have already obtained your PMP certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve managed projects as the assigned “PM” instead of only having delivered them as an engineer. You enjoy the dynamic of wearing multiple hats and taking the lead on client-facing communication, expectations, and timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve owned client-facing projects and have established a consultative rapport resulting in high client satisfaction levels upon project closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have at least 5 years of experience delivering IT waterfall projects working with systems and virtualization with exposure to enterprise infrastructures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You keep us true to our word. You have a tried-and-true organizational system to keep yourself (and others) on task while ensuring exceptional quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You possess a winning combination of superb writing skills and highly refined verbal communication skills. You convey energy, confidence, and genuine interest over a call just as easily as you convey competence, professionalism, and trustworthiness in person. You translate to a C-Suite audience as seamlessly as you “talk tech” with engineers. Your emails are professionally worded, grammatically pristine, with the right pinch of personality. In any medium, you pride yourself in clear, effective, and persuasive communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an approach to working hours that is more adaptable than the traditional &quot;9-to-5&quot;. As this team responds to business-critical remediation projects, we are looking for an individual who is career-driven and won’t shrink back when work requirements extend into evenings, weekends, and holidays. While travel is minimal, you’re also open to getting on a plane when needed to be present at client sites when a project requires it. On the flip side, your hard work is rewarded with a generous comp plan that grows with the efforts you contribute, a flexible PTO policy, and an equally inspiring team that climbs mountains together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are ready to be an effective remote worker and have a dedicated, private space for a home office with a private internet connection with at least 50MBPS bandwidth. Public WiFi and shared common spaces &lt;u&gt;do not&lt;/u&gt; meet these standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Personality Traits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Mythical Character&lt;/strong&gt;. You aren’t alarmed when someone expects you to be a hero; in fact, you pride yourself on frequently delivering big just when all hope seems lost. Your persistence is notable, and you are a determined soul who insists on turning “We can’t” into “We can” If you meet a roadblock, you’ll try to scale it, dodge it, or blast through it before ever admitting defeat.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Devil is in the Details. &lt;/strong&gt;You have an angelic ability to sort through chaos and make order. Your eye and attention for details helps you uncover hidden gems, while your thorough documentation and status updates capture and convey every facet of each stone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Corporate Usain Bolt&lt;/strong&gt;. You’re capable of moving rapidly from task to task without getting rattled. Your desk is clear, your email inbox is empty, your kitchen counters aren’t cluttered, and you never spend 15 minutes tearing around the house in a desperate hunt for your car keys or train pass. You are a lean, mean, well-oiled machine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Combo Meal&lt;/strong&gt;. Your style is winningly ambidextrous. While you are known to be a loyal teammate and never falter on your commitment to seeing others thrive, you are not a push-over. You will fight back and advocate for the best marriage of client desires and superb delivery-pushing us along the path towards perfection. If Samwise Gamgee and Monica Geller had a child, it would be you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emotionally Mature.&lt;/strong&gt; Through your years of experience, you’ve learned that occasional hiccups are inevitable and now know enough to just keep moving towards the end goal. You’re calm under pressure, encourage respectful dialog, and understand that communication is the balm that can soothe the sting of conflict.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The benefits package consists of:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;Generous annual leave entitlement plus bank holidays (pro-rata if part-time working hours apply)&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;Gym discount&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;Life insurance&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;Comprehensive travel insurance for you and your family in line with scheme rules&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;Confidential well-being and counselling support&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;Competitive Compensation&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;Contributory pension scheme&lt;br&gt;•&amp;nbsp;Company events&lt;br&gt;• Private Medical and Dental Insurance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Title: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scrum Master – Software&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced Scrum Master – Software to facilitate Agile software development and help engineering teams deliver high-quality, scalable software solutions. This role serves as a servant leader, Agile coach, and delivery facilitator for one or more cross-functional software development teams. Working closely with Software Engineers, QA Engineers, DevOps Engineers, Solution Architects, Product Owners, and Engineering Managers, the Software Scrum Master ensures the successful execution of Agile ceremonies, removes delivery impediments, improves team performance, and promotes continuous improvement throughout the Software Development Lifecycle (SDLC).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Roles &amp;amp; responsibility:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate Scrum ceremonies including Sprint Planning, Daily Stand-ups, Reviews, Retrospectives, and Backlog Refinement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach teams on Scrum, Agile, and Lean practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Owners to manage backlogs, priorities, and sprint goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track delivery progress, risks, dependencies, and impediments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Engineering, QA, DevOps, Product, and Architecture teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support release planning and continuous improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor Agile metrics and improve team productivity and delivery predictability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate project status, risks, and dependencies to stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in computer science, Information Systems, Software Engineering, Business, or related field, or equivalent professional experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 3 years of experience serving as a Scrum Master supporting software development teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering enterprise software, SaaS platforms, cloud-native applications, or digital products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of Agile software development methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience facilitating Scrum ceremonies for cross-functional engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent leadership, facilitation, coaching, and conflict resolution skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, organizational, and communication abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in fast-paced Agile software environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to work in 24/7 environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CSM, PSM, PMI-ACP, SAFe, or similar certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud/software development environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Jira, Azure DevOps, Confluence, Git, CI/CD, and cloud platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with multiple Agile teams or enterprise applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Overview:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Security Remediation Engineer, you will execute and support Cyber Tier Risk Assessment services, including Microsoft 365 Automated Policy Benchmarking and Vulnerability and Remediation Management. You will own the technical remediation lifecycle for security findings originating from third-party security vendors, internal assessments, and the vulnerability management as a service (VMaaS) engine. This role requires strong hands-on expertise in identifying, testing, implementing, and validating security remediations across modern cloud and enterprise environments. You will articulate remediation outcomes, risks, and tradeoffs to both technical and non-technical stakeholders, ensuring transparency and accuracy throughout delivery. A successful candidate brings deep knowledge of how modern technologies are compromised and secured, and applies that knowledge to deliver reliable, repeatable security improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROLE AND RESPONSIBILITIES &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remediate security vulnerabilities through comprehensive testing and risk forecasting to ensure timely and effective implementation of controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and document standardized processes and procedures for security remediation to ensure consistency and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, manage, and report on remediation requests, providing clear visibility to clients regarding progress and outcomes from vendor-driven engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary escalation point for Security Remediation Engineers, offering guidance and resolving complex technical issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead client-facing calls and presentations to communicate remediation status, address concerns, and align with security objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project manage specialized remediation initiatives and one-off projects originating from CTM team responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze unresolved issues and negative outcomes, recommending process improvements and preventive measures.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain detailed documentation for systems, processes, and remediation workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and drive resolution of pending issues, ensuring accountability and timely closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise stakeholders and translate business requirements into secure, reliable technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and manage email security measures to protect against phishing and other cyber threats.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute vulnerability remediation strategies to identify and mitigate security weaknesses across systems and networks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply and enforce security best practices and industry standards throughout remediation activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and manage cloud services, email security, and baseline hardening, ensuring adherence to standard configurations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5 years of experience in Vulnerability Management &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum 3–4 years of cybersecurity experience in a cloud services environment. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum 3–4 years of experience in a client-facing technology role. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum 3–4 years of experience in a systems engineering position. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience in the financial sector is a plus. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience working at an MSP is a plus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security and/or systems certifications are a plus&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Certifications : &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security and/or systems certifications are a plus &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security+ (nice to have) &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Network+ (nice to have)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MS AZ-500, SC-100, SC-200 (nice to have)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge &amp;amp; Skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ability to design and deliver tailored security technology solutions for clients, ensuring scalability and compliance with industry standards. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven capability to perform under pressure and meet aggressive deadlines, while maintaining accuracy and security integrity. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Highly analytical and logical thinker, skilled in advanced root cause analysis and problem resolution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexibility to occasionally work nights and weekends, with strong prioritization and time management skills. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep technical expertise in public cloud platforms, particularly Microsoft Office 365 and Azure, including advanced configuration and security hardening. • Advanced proficiency in Windows Server technologies, including Active Directory, Group Policy, and Identity Management (Entra/Okta).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Abacus Group, we believe the future of technology services in regulated industries will be defined by the ability to securely operationalize modern infrastructure, cybersecurity, cloud, automation, and AI, not simply deploy tools. The Virtual Technology Manager (VTM) serves as the strategic execution and operational orchestration partner for clients operating in highly regulated environments across Abacus’s Financial Services business unit (hedge funds, private equity firms, RIAs, asset managers, family offices) and Healthcare business unit (hospital and health systems, physician groups, payers, and other regulated healthcare organizations). This role sits at the intersection of technology strategy, operational execution, cybersecurity, infrastructure modernization, cloud services, AI enablement, and service lifecycle management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The VTM works closely with client stakeholders and internal Abacus teams to transform strategic priorities into operational reality by coordinating execution, driving technology adoption, improving operational maturity, and reducing risk across complex client environments. Operating as a trusted technology advisor, the VTM helps align technology decisions to business outcomes while orchestrating delivery across engineering, security, professional services, operations, AI, and client experience teams. Beyond their assigned client engagements, VTMs also execute against Abacus’s catalog of standardized VTM service offerings and technical deliverables, delivering engineering outcomes across the broader client base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VTM engagements follow a portfolio-based or a dedicated assignment model. Portfolio-based VTMs support a range of clients and hours based on business need, while dedicated VTMs are assigned primarily or exclusively to a single client. In either model, the VTM remains an Abacus employee, accountable to Abacus’s standards, operating model, and management structure. The core responsibilities and expectations of the VTM remain consistent across both engagement models, with dedicated assignments providing greater client-specific capacity, continuity, and embedded engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines strong technical depth, operational leadership, executive communication skills, and the ability to coordinate complex initiatives across multiple stakeholders and technologies. This role is ideal for someone looking to move beyond traditional infrastructure management and play a meaningful role in the modernization of technology operations within regulated industries.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is hybrid located in Orlando Florida&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary operational technology partner for assigned clients, developing a deep understanding of each client’s environment, operations, priorities, and technology needs, and aligning infrastructure, cloud, cybersecurity, and emerging technologies to business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary technical liaison between client stakeholders and Abacus delivery teams, ensuring technical needs are clearly understood, appropriately prioritized, and driven through resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform targeted hands-on technical work within the VTM scope while coordinating larger, specialized, or project-based engineering efforts through the appropriate Abacus delivery teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help clients operationalize technology initiatives within regulated environments by supporting infrastructure planning, governance alignment, security, operational readiness, modernization, and adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical guidance and coordinate complex support matters and escalations across Support, Engineering, Security, Infrastructure, AI, Professional Services, Operations, and vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide clients through modernization initiatives involving cloud platforms, cybersecurity, identity and access management, infrastructure lifecycle management, automation, collaboration platforms, and operational tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support clients in evaluating, preparing for, and operationalizing AI-enabled solutions, coordinating specialized AI design and implementation resources where required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve operational maturity, resiliency, scalability, governance, automation, and long-term technology effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain oversight of service activity, recurring concerns, escalations, and technical debt, ensuring ownership, communication, and follow-through, and driving continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain regular engagement with client technical and operational stakeholders through scheduled meetings, ongoing communication, service reviews, and technology planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute against Abacus’s catalog of standardized VTM service offerings and technical deliverables, delivering engineering outcomes across the broader client base beyond one’s own assigned engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For dedicated assignments, operate as an extension of the client’s technology organization while remaining accountable to Abacus’s standards and management structure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ideal Candidate Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience supporting financial services organizations within a managed services, consulting, or enterprise technology environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate effectively with both technical teams and executive stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of infrastructure, cloud, cybersecurity, and operational service delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating complex technical initiatives across multiple teams and vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with regulated environments and compliance-driven operational models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational, communication, and client relationship skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently while driving accountability across matrixed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in AI, automation, and emerging operational technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting financial services organizations, including hedge funds, private equity firms, RIAs, asset managers, and family offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of modern Microsoft-centric infrastructure and cloud ecosystems, including Microsoft 365, Azure, identity, collaboration, and endpoint management platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting hybrid cloud and enterprise infrastructure environments across servers, networking, identity, security, and operational platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of core Microsoft technologies, including Active Directory, Windows Server, Exchange Online, and Entra ID&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cybersecurity, identity and access management, operational modernization, infrastructure lifecycle management, and governance-driven technology environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to AI enablement, governance, automation, or operational modernization initiatives preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience within MSP, MSSP, consulting, Healthcare, or strategic client advisory environments preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting highly regulated or security-sensitive environments strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Abacus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technology services are undergoing a major shift as AI, cloud transformation, cybersecurity, automation, and other emerging technologies continue to reshape regulated industries. Organizations are under increasing pressure to modernize their environments, improve operational maturity, reduce risk, and support evolving business demands in a secure and scalable way.&amp;nbsp;At Abacus Group, we serve as a strategic technology partner for financial services and healthcare organizations, helping clients modernize, secure, operate, and continuously improve complex technology environments. This role offers the opportunity to work directly with sophisticated financial services clients while helping drive infrastructure modernization, cybersecurity maturity, operational effectiveness, and the adoption of emerging technologies like AI across highly regulated environments.&amp;nbsp;If you want to help regulated organizations operationalize the future of technology, we should talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
