&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Title: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support Engineer – Software&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Support Engineer – Software&lt;/strong&gt; to provide technical support for enterprise software applications. The role will troubleshoot application, database, API, and integration issues while working closely with Engineering, Product, DevOps, and Customer Success teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Roles &amp;amp; responsibility:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide L2/L3 technical support for enterprise and SaaS applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot application, database, API, integration, and system issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze logs, reproduce defects, identify root causes, and provide solutions or workarounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage incidents and service requests according to SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate complex issues to Engineering with detailed technical analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Development, QA, Product, and DevOps teams on production issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support deployments, upgrades, patches, and release validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain troubleshooting guides, knowledge articles, and technical documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor application health and identify recurring issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in on-call support as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent professional experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–5 years of experience in technical support, application support, software engineering, or IT operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting enterprise or SaaS applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of client/server architecture, web applications, REST APIs, and networking fundamentals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with SQL databases and writing basic to intermediate SQL queries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Windows and Linux operating systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using ticketing systems such as Jira, ServiceNow, Zendesk, or similar platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent troubleshooting, analytical, and critical thinking skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize multiple issues in a fast-paced environment while maintaining a high level of customer service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work in a 24/7 environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred skills &amp;amp; experience &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Docker, Kubernetes, CI/CD, and DevOps practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with monitoring tools such as Splunk, Datadog, Grafana, or New Relic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic scripting knowledge in PowerShell, Bash, or Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with authentication protocols such as OAuth, SAML, or LDAP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ITIL Foundation certification is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

